{"id":"b4","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":5,"of":17,"title":"The word with no meaning","titleHe":"אֶת","goal":"Use אֶת before a definite direct object.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"אֶת has no translation. It marks the direct object of a verb — but only when that object is definite. It's one of the commonest words in Hebrew and one of the last a learner uses correctly."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי רוֹאֶה בַּיִת.","en":"I see a house. — no אֶת"},{"he":"אֲנִי רוֹאֶה אֶת הַבַּיִת.","en":"I see the house. — definite, so אֶת"},{"he":"הִיא אוֹהֶבֶת אֶת דָּוִד.","en":"She loves David. — names are definite"}]},{"type":"text","body":"With a pronoun it declines, and those forms are how you say me, him, them as objects."},{"type":"table","caption":"אֶת with endings","head":["","form"],"rows":[["me","אוֹתִי"],["you (m.)","אוֹתְךָ"],["you (f.)","אוֹתָךְ"],["him / it","אוֹתוֹ"],["her","אוֹתָהּ"],["us","אוֹתָנוּ"],["them","אוֹתָם"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֶת","en":"(marks a definite object)","translit":"et"},{"he":"אוֹתִי","en":"me","translit":"oti"},{"he":"אוֹתוֹ","en":"him, it","translit":"oto"},{"he":"אוֹתָהּ","en":"her","translit":"ota"},{"he":"רוֹאֶה","en":"sees","translit":"ro'e"},{"he":"שׁוֹמֵעַ","en":"hears","translit":"shome'a"},{"he":"יוֹדֵעַ","en":"knows","translit":"yode'a"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["size","decides","(marks a definite object)","always"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אֶת","translit":"et"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["new","long","me","storm"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אוֹתִי","translit":"oti"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sells, a seller","him, it","the same thing","kitchen"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אוֹתוֹ","translit":"oto"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in order to","salvation","vision","her"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אוֹתָהּ","translit":"ota"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["to him","concerning","bud","sees"],"correct":3,"prompt":"רוֹאֶה","translit":"ro'e"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["world","hears","fifty","Sukkot"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שׁוֹמֵעַ","translit":"shome'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["table","there isn't","building","knows"],"correct":3,"prompt":"יוֹדֵעַ","translit":"yode'a"},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"הִיא ___ אֶת דָּוִד.","en":"She loves David. — names are definite","options":["אֶת","אוֹהֶבֶת","רוֹאֶה","יוֹדֵעַ"],"correct":1,"full":"הִיא אוֹהֶבֶת אֶת דָּוִד."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “hears”?","options":["מַשְׂכֹּרֶת","נָעִים","עוֹמֵד","שׁוֹמֵעַ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"them?","options":["אוֹתְךָ","אוֹתָם","אוֹתִי","אוֹתָךְ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אֶת","(marks a definite object)"],["אוֹתִי","me"],["אוֹתוֹ","him, it"],["אוֹתָהּ","her"],["רוֹאֶה","sees"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"you (m.)?","options":["אוֹתִי","אוֹתוֹ","אוֹתְךָ","אוֹתָךְ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"us?","options":["אוֹתָךְ","אוֹתָנוּ","אוֹתְךָ","אוֹתִי"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “him, it”?","options":["אוֹתוֹ","אֹכֶל","אֶת","דְּבַשׁ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"רוֹאֶה","translit":"ro'e","en":"sees"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “me” in Hebrew","answer":"אוֹתִי","hint":"oti"}]}